      "mergedPostDetails": "So I was having a quick look through the guidelines and I was a bit confused on some of the information given and why those numbers were chosen.\n\nI honestly think this is what your guidelines should be and I'll provide reasoning to this as well.\n\n1.Skin mesh render: 2 \n\nReason: There is no need to have multiple skin meshes this would tell you they have even gone over the unity poly import limit and they have had to separate parts to make the tri count lower so they can have face visemes. Honestly you guys should increase the tri limit to 65k at this point anyway as thats unitys max. But point being thats why theres so many mesh renders. Also particle effect shows shouldnt be on public avatars this is due to overuse and spamming in public worlds.\n\n2. Dyn bone: 10 scripts maximum on character and must set to Animate Physics.\n\nReason: Count as scripts not how many bones there is no more of a draw count with bones vs script. Theres an issue with counting them that includes the radius distribution as individual bones. Example: I have 3 bones for the hair but set radius distribution to 0.00015 to get better flow between the bones but it counts the bones as 40 bones instead of three bones. Animate Physics is a good option seems to be more optimised less draw calls than normal. I think its because it uses the mesh information with the bone instead of trying to create physics from the bone itself? more information is required but I've experienced more draw calls using normal on the script.\n\n3. Dyn Colliders: 10 scripts \n\nReason: I think 10 is a round number drawcalls for 10 scripts of colliders is 20 anymore than that is overkill. This also helps out those who are using long hair and/or dresses. Maybe make it subjective to the model so for instance if it doesnt need colliders then deny that avatar.\n\n\n4. Materials: 10 \n\n\nReason: Honestly if you have more than 10 materials you're looking at over 50 calls. Mats are more expensive than colliders. you should have at max 1-2 for face (TDA have their mesh split in the centre) 1 for clothes 1 for transparents 1 for hair. Anymore than that is overkill.\n\n\n(New) 5. Maximum custom shaders: 4 \n\nReason: Not including whitelisted shaders but any other custom shader should be limited to 4 on a public avatar shaders can also be pretty darn expensive. As such non whitelisted shaders should be  kept down to 4 maximum.\n\nI think some people may have posted something similar if they have feel free to merge.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Avatar world guideline request to change",
